{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7702","id":5211682188,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNqP1jA","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7702","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7702.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7702.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7702","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7702/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7702/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7702/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/30d851688446b048d56cd1ba6c98bbd4966d2ff0","number":7702,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(id): reject duplicate JSON fields in world_fixture headers and events (#6474)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What\n\nFixes #6474. `world_fixture::decode_header` and `decode_event` parsed each JSON Lines record into `serde_json::Value` with plain `serde_json::from_str`, which collapses duplicate keys last-wins **before** `check_keys`, the fixture version gate, nested `records` parsing, or `check_window` can look at the text. A fixture line could therefore name two worlds, hide an unsupported `fixture` version behind a supported one, repeat a nested `records` key, or hide an out-of-window `sequence` — and every check would validate only the surviving value.\n\nQueue task: `repo-health-code-pilot` task **12995** (issue #6474).\n\n## Changes\n\n- `pkgs/id/src/world_fixture.rs`\n  - `decode_header` and `decode_event` now parse through the shared rejecting parser `crate::world_session::parse_json_without_duplicate_keys` (landed in #6508), so a duplicate key is a parse error at any nesting depth.\n  - Error context is unchanged: header failures still read `the fixture header is not JSON`, event failures `the event is not JSON`, and both still carry the `fixture line N` context added by the caller.\n- `pkgs/id/src/world_fixture.rs` tests\n  - New `decode_refuses_duplicate_fields_in_the_header_and_events` covers: duplicate `world`, an unsupported `fixture` version hidden behind a supported one, a nested duplicate `records` key, an out-of-window duplicate event `sequence` (asserting the `fixture line 2` context), and a valid control that still decodes.\n\nNo wire, journal, or shell-contract change: this only makes an already-invalid input fail at parse time instead of being silently collapsed.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cd pkgs/id && cargo test --lib world_fixture::tests::decode_refuses` — 4 passed (includes the new duplicate-key case and the existing malformed/version/window suites).\n- Formatting is auto-fixed on main per `.github/ci-policy.md`; no treefmt gate.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796736287&installation_model_id=443529&pr_